    21	 *     stderr.
    22	 *
    23	 * Output/exit contract (bounded by the CLI engine, which prints the handler
    24	 * return and forces exit 0 on a normal return):
    25	 *   - text mode, success -> host stdout already streamed live; RETURN '' (nothing
    26	 *     to re-print), usage line to stderr, process exit 0;
    27	 *   - text mode, host failure / cap refusal -> host output already streamed;
    28	 *     usage/refusal line to stderr, THROW a concise error so the process exits
    29	 *     nonzero (the exact host code + refusal reason are in the message);
    30	 *   - json mode -> RETURN the structured result (exitCode, usage, refusal, the
